comments.body:
Confirming here as the author of the `hunt76-a-websearch-citations` branch: upstream `1d6b72ad` (in a release since v0.1.1369) covers this issue. @HuHong-Tao's field test on 0.1.1371 above is the proof — citations now arrive both streamed (`citations_delta` ahead of the text) and whole, with real excerpts in `cited_text` on the search-for path.

For the record, the two approaches took different roads to the same place: upstream builds the citations from the page URLs the model cites in its own answer ("Cite the URLs you use"), while the two fork branches (mine and skygunner's) synthesized them from the search results' excerpts. With the upstream version shipped, neither fork branch is needed anymore — both are archived as obsolete.

@yetone since the reporter has verified the fix, this issue can be closed. Thanks again @HuHong-Tao for the thorough verification!

